 "honest": [
  "the churn sleeve is an equal-weight mean over the swapped names, not a portfolio return: it says whether the names taken in beat the names given up inside that window, not how much money the book made",
  "both calendars share one calendar, one universe and one rank cache, so the only moving part is the set of decision sessions",
  "mid-month is a single fixed date (day 15), not a sweep: it prices a wrong-calendar cost, it does not search for a better one",
  "the fee_gap figure is an order-of-magnitude conversion of the turnover difference into bp/yr, not a reconciliation of the measured gap",
  "descriptive census only: no gate, no verdict, no prereg, no trial count"
 ]
